<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/calculator.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/calculator-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/calculator.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.12"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/claim-toolbox/">Claim toolbox</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Claim Gap &amp; Net Recovery Estimator</span></nav><p class="tag">Free estimator · runs in your browser</p><h1>Claim Gap and Net Recovery Estimator</h1><p class="lede">Enter the carrier’s number and yours, pick where an award might land, and add realistic fees. The estimator shows your net at a cautious, middle and strong outcome so you can judge whether appraisal pays.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool" data-tool="gap">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Claim gap &amp; net recovery estimator</span><i>Runs in your browser</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="g-ins">Insurer’s estimate (RCV)</label><input id="g-ins" name="insurer" inputmode="decimal" value="22600"><span class="hint">Replacement cost total on the carrier’s estimate.</span></div>
        <div><label for="g-own">Your estimate (RCV)</label><input id="g-own" name="yours" inputmode="decimal" value="38900"><span class="hint">Your contractor’s or independent estimate.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div><label for="g-land">Where might the award land inside the gap?</label>
        <div class="range"><input id="g-land" type="range" name="land" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="55" data-unit="%"><output>55%</output></div>
        <span class="hint">0% means the carrier’s number holds. 100% means your full number is awarded.</span></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="g-ft">Your appraiser’s fee type</label><select id="g-ft" name="feetype"><option value="flat">Flat fee ($)</option><option value="pct">Percent of increase (%)</option><option value="hourly">Hourly (hours × rate)</option></select></div>
        <div><label for="g-fee">Fee amount, % or hours</label><input id="g-fee" name="fee" inputmode="decimal" value="2800"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="g-rate">Hourly rate (if hourly)</label><input id="g-rate" name="rate" inputmode="decimal" value="175"></div>
        <div><label for="g-ump">Umpire’s total fee</label><input id="g-ump" name="umpire" inputmode="decimal" value="3500"></div>
      </div>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="useump" checked> <span>An umpire will be needed (you pay half)</span></label>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="out-big"><small>Estimated net increase to you</small><b data-o="net">$0</b></div>
      <div class="stack" aria-hidden="true"><span class="s-a"></span><span class="s-b"></span><span class="s-c"></span></div>
      <div class="legend"><span><i class="s-a"></i>Carrier’s number</span><span><i class="s-b"></i>Your net gain</span><span><i class="s-c"></i>Appraisal costs</span></div>
      <div class="out-rows">
        <div><span>Amount in dispute</span><b data-o="gap">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Gap as % of carrier estimate</span><b data-o="pct">—</b></div>
        <div><span>Projected award (RCV)</span><b data-o="award">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Gross increase</span><b data-o="gain">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Your appraisal costs</span><b data-o="cost">$0</b></div>
      </div>
      <div class="scen"><p class="todo-h">Net at three outcomes</p>
        <div class="scen-row"><span>Cautious (30%)</span><b data-o="s30">$0</b></div>
        <div class="scen-row"><span>Middle (55%)</span><b data-o="s55">$0</b></div>
        <div class="scen-row"><span>Strong (80%)</span><b data-o="s80">$0</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="out-msg" data-o="msg"></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint tool-hint">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice, and nothing you type is stored.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>How to use it</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Enter the insurer’s RCV total</strong>, the replacement cost figure before depreciation and deductible.</li>
<li><strong>Enter your estimate</strong> at replacement cost too, so you compare like with like.</li>
<li><strong>Pick a fee arrangement.</strong> Flat, percentage and hourly fees are all common. Use the terms you’ve actually been quoted.</li>
<li><strong>Read the three outcomes.</strong> If appraisal only pays off at the strong outcome, the case is fragile.</li></ol>
<h2>Example figures</h2>
<p>The starting numbers are illustrative only. They don’t come from any real claim or client.</p>
<h2>What the estimator leaves out</h2>
<p>Deductibles, depreciation timing and policy limits affect what you’re paid, not the size of the dispute. For holdback math, use the <a href="/claim-toolbox/acv-holdback-calculator/">ACV &amp; holdback calculator</a>.</p>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is the projected award a prediction?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="ans"><p>No. It’s a planning scenario. Real awards depend on documentation, the panel and the policy.</p></div></details><details><summary>Why show three outcomes?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="ans"><p>Awards rarely match either side’s opening number. Looking at a range shows whether appraisal still makes sense if the panel accepts only part of your estimate.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="related"><a class="rel" href="/claim-toolbox/acv-holdback-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small>ACV &amp; Holdback Calculator<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/claim-toolbox/roof-pitch-squares-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small>Roof Pitch &amp; Squares Calculator<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/claim-toolbox/hurricane-deductible-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small>Hurricane Deductible Calculator<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="f